        "original_id": "d12e66ba-6a1a-5600-ab74-bffca99ecd57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Serena Williams, Mariaan de Swardt, Samantha Stosur\n- Sports: women's tennis\n- Events: 1992 Summer Olympics, 1996 Summer Olympics, South African Fed Cup Team, 2011 Rogers Cup – Women's Singles\n\nFacts:\n- Mariaan de Swardt was born on 18 March 1971 and is a former tennis player from South Africa.\n- Mariaan de Swardt played professional tennis from 1988 to 2001.\n- Mariaan de Swardt represented South Africa at the Summer Olympics in 1992 and 1996.\n- Mariaan de Swardt was a member of the South African Fed Cup Team in 1992 and from 1994 to 1997.\n- Serena Jameka Williams was born on September 26, 1981 and is an American professional tennis player.\n- Serena Williams became the world No. 1 for the first time on July 8, 2002.\n- Serena Williams won the 2011 Rogers Cup – Women's Singles title by defeating Samantha Stosur 6–4, 6–2 in the final.",
